  "synthesis_conclusions": [
    "Population density significantly affected soundscape perception (PAQ ratings) and physiological responses (EEG alpha power) in urban environments.",
    "Busy Plazas and empty Parks effectively evoked positive emotional states (joy and serenity) in participants.",
    "Urban Plazas, especially when occupied, should be considered valuable tools in urban soundscape design, similar to parks.",
    "Increased population density led to higher Eventful PAQ ratings across all locations, while Calm and Pleasant PAQ ratings decreased.",
    "Higher EEG alpha power in empty locations with natural sounds suggests increased relaxation, corroborating previous findings on restorative environments.",
    "Educational level may influence EEG responses to soundscapes, with highly educated individuals showing more consistent brain activity patterns."
  ],
  "evidence_gaps": [
    "Further investigation of EEG results with neuroscience experts is needed.",
    "Continued enhancement and validation of PAQ translations into Portuguese and other languages.",
    "Replication of EEG-VR soundscape experiments in different cultural contexts (e.g., Brazil).",
    "Determination of an optimized number of people to evoke well-being in urban soundscapes.",
    "Validation of whether children's sounds are a significant influencing factor for Vibrant soundscapes.",
    "Observation of the relationship between memory and soundscape perception.",
    "New investigations controlling audio and visual stimuli to determine if alpha power increases in occipital regions are related to soundscapes, visual cues, or both."
  ],
